would-be asylum seekers who tried to  cross the border into the european union  are reportedly facing illegal and  violent pushbacks  new investigations using video  recordings and documents show an alleged  campaign orchestrated by special police  units in croatia greece and romania to  forcibly keep migrants out  at croatia's border with  bosnia-herzegovina investigative  journalists found systematic use of  force by special police units funded by  the european union now as  a member of the european union croatia  is required to allow any migrant  entering there to apply for asylum in  the eu  allegations of so-called pushbacks have  been circulating for years journalists  filmed this incident earlier this year  the footage shows masked men in uniform  and armed with batons beating would-be  asylum seekers apparently to stop them  from entering the european union  one of the masked men could be heard  shouting go to bosnia  the group of asylum seekers were from  pakistan and afghanistan  medics from doctors without borders  later treated their injuries and said  that they were consistent with being  being struck with batons  the masked men did not wear badges but  they used equipment that active and  former officers say is the same as  croatia's  border police  well my next guest tonight is a  journalist with lighthouse reports which  has been at the forefront of  investigating what it calls the shadow  armies on the eu's borders klaus van  dyken is an award-winning war  correspondent who filmed that striking  video that we've just seen colossus good  to have you  on the program before we start i just  want to share with our viewers what you  tweeted today  you posted hiding in the trees listening  to the damp thwack of batons on human  bodies the screams will be hard to  forget as has been the case with  reporting from conflict zones it becomes  more troubling with distance and  reflection  there's a powerful words there class  talk us through what you saw on the  border  it started um i think with um  entering the the area  where these pushbacks are are happening  um and we know we knew or we found out  where where the exact spots were  and um  we  we had to crawl through through the  forest basically um  and hide there and wait um and then at  some point we we heard a car coming uh  from from the other side of a river  um and  the the slamming doors um and that was  on the croatian side so we were on the  boston inside hiding um in in in the  forest  um and then the first thing that i heard  were with the beatings  and i think we were  well less than 30 meters away um but  still it's it's quite a distance but  then when you hear the beatings and the  screamings and that are coming out of  the  uh from the other side of the river and  yeah that's that's um quite shocking um  and then we saw people jumping in to the  river and they were forced into the  river by by these guys wearing dark  uniforms and balaclavas on their faces  and clouds how did you know where  to wait and when to wait  uh where is that we we work with a with  a team of journalists um of from all  over over europe um and there have been  people building up a network um along  the border uh with just local contacts  who helped out to to tell because a lot  of people know where where these things  are happening  um and um they were they were able to  give us directions um and to to point us  to to the places where we had to wait  and then it was also uh just just luck  um so sometimes something happens and  then other other times  um yeah we had to wait for days and  sometimes nights and nothing happened  the european union's executive has  voiced serious concern over the pushback  reports and has called for  investigations in greece and croatia  here's the eu's home affairs  commissioner speaking earlier today take  a listen  i must say that the croatian government  takes this very seriously they were  going to immediately investigate the  minister was shocked and i think they  are doing exactly the right thing  my discussion with the greek minister  was different and i have made clear that  i will not accept that greece do not  do the investigations on this we have to  protect our external borders but we also  have to protect our values the rule of  law and fundamental rights  so what do you make of what you just  heard there you know she said that the  minister was shocked do you buy that  and not for a second um they know  exactly what what is going on and also  uh people in the european union or the  european uh the eu commissioners they  they also know that this this is going  on and they knew it for for a long time  already there have been reports um from  from uh from journalists ngos activists  um  and but this is the first time that  there is visual evidence of it so they  could not longer deny it  and yeah that's that's why this material  is is important that it's out there  um  to so tonight croatia  said that they suspended three officers  that apparently were seen in the video  um although we we  saw four video four men in in the video  but they found three of them and they  did it within within half a day um so on  all the other reports that are there on  all the other violations they it's it's  very easy apparently for them to just  find the officers and investigate  okay but this is the first time to  actually do it  klaus van dyken journalist with  lighthouse reports klaus we appreciate  your reporting we'll be following this  story we know you will be come back and  talk with us when there are new  developments thank you  thank you so much  you
 

